Let a language server finish saving its state before coc exits

Vim stops coc by sending SIGTERM to its whole process group, which kills the
language servers before they get the LSP `shutdown`. Spawning them `detached`
(on the spawn call only, so coc still force-kills a hung server after 2 s)
leaves the signal to node, whose `gracefulExit` then shuts them down properly.
Keeping node alive for the full `EXIT_TIMEOUT`, raised to 5 s, gives that
shutdown and the force-kill time to finish.

